# R05-P2-04: GEMINI_API_KEY is NOT a client secret any more.
#
# The Android app used to compile this key into the APK and append it to a request URL, so anyone
# with the APK could extract and spend it. Gemini is now called only from Cloud Functions, which
# reads the key from Secret Manager:
#
#   firebase functions:secrets:set GEMINI_API_KEY
#
# Do not add it to this file: the Secrets Gradle Plugin publishes every property here as a
# BuildConfig field, i.e. straight into the APK.

# MAPS_API_KEY: Required to display Google Maps tiles.
# Obtain a key from https://console.cloud.google.com/ and enable the Maps SDK for Android.
# Restrict the key to package `com.aistudio.skillsexchange.nxptvq` + your signing SHA-1.
# Without a valid key the app will show a "Map unavailable" fallback instead of crashing.
# Set this in your local .env file — never commit a real key to version control.
MAPS_API_KEY=DEFAULT_MAPS_API_KEY
